I have no idea where you're coming unstuck. I have 3.4.3 
built-from-source with dual TTY & Qt windowports.
http://members.ozemail.com.au/~martincrisp/dual_nethack.png

I'm on Mac OS X 10.2.8, with gcc -v returning:
Thread model: posix
Apple Computer, Inc. GCC version 1175, based on gcc version 3.1 
20020420 (prerelease)


[I used Qt/Mac Free 3.3.0b1 initially, found it had a problem with 
sound, went to 3.2.3 and that was fine. A later snapshot of Qt/Mac 
Free 3.3.0b1 worked fine.]

These are the changes I made to the source to build [for you and 
any other interested]:
unixconf.h:
  enabled the define of BSD (removed trailing '1')
  commented the defines of SYSV and SVR4
system.h
  changed an unsigned int to an unsigned long because of a conflict
  with an apple-supplied header. (about line 83)
top-level Makefile
  changed PREFIX, GAMEUID, GAMEGRP
  PREFIX=/Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS
  GAMEUID= root
  GAMEGRP=admin
  [the same as for Apple-supplied applications - I should probably
  have set SECURE, but didn't... comments sought]
/src/Makefile
  uncommented the CC=gcc line ("to be sure, to be sure" according
  to the comment I added above; same in util/Makefile)
  uncommented the LINK=g++ line [install.qt refers to previous
  source where this was LD=g++]
  made the WINTTYLIB=-lncurses, disabled the existing
  other changes as specified in install.qt [for WINQTOBJ, WINQTLIB,
  WINQTSRC, VARDATND]
include/config.h
  uncommented the define of QT_GRAPHICS
  changed the define of HACKDIR to
  "/Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS/lib/nethackdir"
  uncommented the define of AUTOPICKUP_EXCEPTIONS
  
Before proceeding to make, I created an empty folder in 
/Applications/ named 'NetHack'

Then from the NetHack source top level directory:
went to the src directory: 
make
back to top level: 
make
sudo make install
<supply admin password>

my .tcshrc specifies /usr/games/ in my $PATH, so:
cd /usr/games
sudo ln -fs 
/Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents/MacOS/nethack ./nethack

At this point TTY worked, but the Qt side still wasn't a Mac 
application 'bundle'. 

Inside /Applications/NetHack/NetHack.app/Contents
   put a copy of Info.plist
   
   made a "Frameworks" folder, and copied the
   $QTDIR/lib/libqt.3.2.3.dylib into it, then renamed that lib to
   libqt.dylib
   
   made a "Resources" folder, copied nethack.icns to it

[Note: I had an existing Qt install that had the first and last of 
these, so I copied those, rather than using the ones in the source 
distrib, it was more convenient for me. This done at the 
commandline with sudo, because the dirs were chown'd to root during 
install]   
   
Checked that everything was owned by root, and in group admin.

Voila: it worked (other than sound, as noted above & since fixed).

Copied existing bones, save, logfile, record into appropriate 
places. 

